        {
          "id": "eb129585-c150-43e3-8774-aadf7d1dd69a",
          "name": "Get Daily Closing Price time series.",
          "request": {
            "name": "Get Daily Closing Price time series.",
            "description": {
              "content": "Closing price generally refers to the last price at which a stock trades during a regular trading session.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "direct-web-services",
                "time-series",
                "v1",
                "reference",
                "daily-closing-price",
                ":ids"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "idTypes",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "\nComma-separated list specifying the type of each value passed in the `ids` parameter.<br>\nRules:\n\n*   Values must align with the order of values in `ids`\n*   Use empty entries to skip\n*   Omit trailing commas after the last non-empty value\n*   Empty values default to `performanceId`\n\nExample:\n\n*   `ids=id1,id2,id3`\n*   `id1` and `id3` are performance IDs\n*   `id2` is a security ID\n*   `idTypes=,securityId`\n\nAccepted values:\n\n*   `performanceId` (default)\n*   `isin`\n*   `securityId`\n*   `cusip`\n*   `tradingSymbol`\n*   `msid`"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "baseCurrency",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "\nComma-separated list of 3-character ISO 4217 currency codes (for example, `CAD`, `EUR`, `JPY`).<br>\n\n*   Filters results based on currency\n*   Values must align with the order of values in `ids`\n*   Use empty entries to skip\n*   Omit trailing commas after the last non-empty value\n\nExample:\n\n*   `ids=id1,id2,id3,id4,id5`\n*   Base currency passed for `id2` and `id4`\n*   `baseCurrency=,USD,,USD`"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "domicile",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "\nComma-separated list of 3-character ISO 3166‑1 country codes (for example, `CAN`, `IRL`, `IND`). \nRules:\n\n*   Filters results based on domicile\n*   Values must align with the order of values in `ids`\n*   Use empty entries to skip\n*   Omit trailing commas after the last non-empty value\n\nExample:\n\n*   `ids=id1,id2,id3,id4,id5`\n*   Domicile passed for `id2` and `id4`\n*   `domicile=,USA,,USA`"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "exchangeCountry",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "\nComma-separated list of 3-character ISO 3166‑1 country codes (for example, `CAN`, `IRL`, `IND`).\n\n\n*   Filters results based on domicile\n*   Values must align with the order of values in `ids`\n*   Use empty entries to skip\n*   Omit trailing commas after the last non-empty value\n\nExample:\n\n*   `ids=id1,id2,id3,id4,id5`\n*   Exchange country passed for `id2` and `id4`\n*   `exchangeCountry=,USA,,USA`"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "exchangeId",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "\nComma-separated list of exchange IDs (for example, `EX$$$$XMEX`, `EX$$$$XNAS`).\n\n*   Filters results based on exchange ID\n*   Values must align with the order of values in `ids`\n*   Use empty entries to skip\n*   Omit trailing commas after the last non-empty value\n\nExample:\n\n*   `ids=id1,id2,id3,id4,id5`\n*   Exchange ID passed for `id2` and `id4`\n*   `exchangeId=,EX$$$$XMEX,,EX$$$$XNAS`"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "frequency",
                  "value": "daily",
                  "description": "Specifies the time interval between data points."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "startDate",
                  "value": "<date>",
                  "description": "Specifies the start date for the time series. Accepted format is `yyyy-MM-dd`.\n"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "endDate",
                  "value": "<date>",
                  "description": "Specifies the end date for the time series. Accepted format is `yyyy-MM-dd`.\n"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "timePeriod",
                  "value": "<number>",
                  "description": "Specifies the size of the time window for the data range. \n\n- Used in combination with `timePeriodUnit` to specify relative time ranges. \n\n- When `startDate`, `endDate`, `timePeriod` and `timePeriodUnit` are provided, `timePeriod` and `timePeriodUnit` take precedence."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "timePeriodUnit",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "\nSpecifies the time period unit. \n\n- Used in combination with `timePeriod` to specify relative time ranges. \n\n- When `startDate`, `endDate`, `timePeriod` and `timePeriodUnit` are provided, `timePeriod` and `timePeriodUnit` take precedence."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "applyEarliestCommonDate",
                  "value": "false",
                  "description": "\nSpecifies whether to apply the earliest common start date across all investments.\n\n When set to `true`, the start date of the time series is adjusted to match the latest inception date among the investments, ensuring all data points are aligned."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "applyTrackRecordExtension",
                  "value": "false",
                  "description": "\nSpecifies whether to apply the Track Record Extension logic in order to extend the performance of an investment by copying the historical performance of another qualified older investment."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "applyRestructureDate",
                  "value": "false",
                  "description": "\nSpecifies whether to consider the Morningstar or Custom restructure date when determining the start of the performance period.\n\nThis option is applicable only when `applyEarliestCommonDate` is set to true."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "sinceInception",
                  "value": "false",
                  "description": "\nSets the time range from inception (or the maximum supported lookback) to the end date. \n\nTakes precendence over any `timePeriod` / `timePeriodUnit` and `startDate` / `endDate` settings."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "currencyId",
                  "value": "BASE",
                  "description": "Specifies the currency in which to return data."
                }
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "key": "ids",
                  "description": "(Required) \nComma-separated list of up to 25 investment identifiers to query.\n\nAccepts:\n\n- Morningstar Performance ID (default)\n- Morningstar Security ID\n- Morningstar IDs (MSID)\n- ISIN\n- CUSIP\n- Trading symbol\n- Category ID   \n  Important: When a category ID is passed, the corresponding `identifierType` can be `performanceId` or `securityId`. The value must be URL-encoded. For example, if the category ID is `LC00002226;CA]FO`, the URL-encoded value is `LC00002226;CA%5DFO`."
                }
              ]
            },
